From 8dca15190798a4b8bcf91f39980077e95301500e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:27:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1124: Implement gpuagent UBB node power

Re-introduce UBB (node) power from amdsmi_get_power_info() -> ubb_power
only, for GPUGet and GPUWatch, without amdsmi_get_node_handle /
amdsmi_get_npm_info (render node waker, ROCM-26020).

- proto/API: GPU_WATCH_ATTR_ID_UBB_POWER = 140, AGA_GPU_WATCH_ATTRS_MAX
  141, svc proto<->aga id mapping, unit "Watts"
- amdsmi: create-time probe on partition 0 records g_ubb_power_gpus;
  GPUGet fills stats->ubb_power only for probed handles; 0 and
  UINT32_MAX map to UINT64_MAX (N/A, never 0)
- gpu_entry::fill_stats_ presets ubb_power = UINT64_MAX (parents, gim,
  wsl, children)
- watcher: attr 140 in k_fast_attrs; amdsmi case reads power_info for
  probed handles; gim/wsl cases publish UINT64_MAX; reset to N/A each
  tick via aga_gpu_watch_reset_fast_fields
- mock: synthetic ubb_power on partition 0

Attr 140 has a 1 s supported-cadence floor (GPUOP-1108 comment 592985).
At today's 1 s fast tick it is read once per tick. GPUOP-1122 owns the
per-attribute cadence mechanism and must gate this read to at most once
per 1 s on sub-second ticks and carry the value forward instead of the
per-tick reset (hook points commented in smi_state.cc and
aga_gpu_watch.hpp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
